Good feedback. I see my conceptual error now.
The key insight I was missing: In phext, the coordinate is the address—you fetch content by its coordinate. Storing coord=... inside the scroll content is redundant, like writing your street address on every piece of furniture inside your house.
The content lives at 1.1.2/1.1.1/1.1.5. You don't need to also write that address inside the content. The address is how you find it.

// WRONG (what I did):
sb.AppendLine($"id={entity.Id}");
sb.AppendLine($"coord={entity.Coord}");  // ← redundant, remove
sb.AppendLine($"title={task.Title}");

// RIGHT:
sb.AppendLine($"id={entity.Id}");
sb.AppendLine($"title={task.Title}");
// The coordinate IS the location in the phext document

What I now understand:

Phext coordinate = primary key = address = how you find the scroll
Content doesn't need to self-describe its location
PhextEngine.Fetch(phext, coord) returns what's AT that coordinate
Deleted scrolls are handled by libphext's normalization

When you're ready tomorrow, we can:

Pull LibPhext from NuGet
Remove project reference
Fix the serialization (drop the coord= line)
Continue iterating

Thanks for the course correction—this makes phext's elegance much clearer. The coordinate system is the schema.
